SUMMARY:🍁🎄Fall Niagara Falls Hiking Day Trip — Trails\, Dinner & F
 estival of Lights!!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍁🎄 Niagara Falls Fall Hiki
 ng Trip & Winter Festival of Lights! 🌈\n\n🌦️ **RAIN OR SHINE!**\n\
 nThe adventure goes on\, whether we're enjoying golden sunshine\, crisp au
 tumn air\, or a little mist from the Falls. After a day of hiking\, we'll 
 finish with dinner and the spectacular Winter Festival of Lights! ✨\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🥾 About the Trip\n\nLet's escape the city for a full day of fr
 esh air\, friendship\, and breathtaking scenery! We'll explore the natural
  side of Niagara Falls — less time in the tourist crowds\, more trails\,
  trees\, and spectacular views.\n\nWe'll meet outside the **Fairmont Royal
  York on Front Street West**\, travel together by GO Train to Niagara Fall
 s\, and make our way to **Niagara Glen Nature Reserve** for a hike among a
 ncient boulders\, winding forest paths\, and the turquoise waters of the N
 iagara River.\n\nThe trail features stairs\, uneven ground\, elevation cha
 nges\, and a climb back up out of the gorge. This is a proper hike\, so pl
 ease read the expectations below before signing up.\n\n**A Special Guest J
 oining Us!**\n\nWe're excited to welcome Miles Howard\, visiting us from B
 oston on November 14–15!\n\nMiles is writing *HIKE EVERY CITY*\, a book 
 (coming in 2028) exploring urban hiking\, community\, and how exploring ci
 ties on foot brings people together. He also runs a similar urban hiking p
 roject in Boston called *Walking City Trails*.\n\nHe'll be joining us for 
 both weekend outings\, including Niagara Falls\, to experience our group f
 irsthand and meet our members.\nFeel free to say hello\, share your experi
 ences\, and chat with Miles if you'd like. No pressure\, of course!\n\nIt'
 s exciting to see our community getting noticed beyond Toronto. Let's give
  Miles a warm welcome!\n\n***\n\n## 🌲 The Trail Experience\n\nNiagara G
 len is a beautiful natural area carved into the Niagara Gorge over thousan
 ds of years. We'll follow forest trails\, take photos\, enjoy the fall col
 ours\, and experience a side of Niagara Falls that many visitors never see
 .\n\nThe planned hike is approximately **4 km**\, although the terrain mak
 es it more demanding than the distance might suggest. We'll have opportuni
 ties to pause and enjoy the scenery\, but everyone needs to be prepared fo
 r the physical demands of the route.\n\n### ⚠️🥾 IMPORTANT: HIKE EXP
 ECTATIONS — PLEASE READ CAREFULLY 🥾⚠️\n\n**This is a real hiking 
 trail\, not a casual walk.**\nBefore signing up\, please be confident that
  you can:\n\n* ✔️ Walk for an extended period of time.\n* ✔️ Handl
 e uneven terrain\, stairs\, elevation changes\, and the climb back up out 
 of the gorge.\n* ✔️ Keep up with the group at a steady pace without ne
 eding frequent or extended stops.\n* ✔️ Manage a full day of walking\,
  travel\, dinner\, and evening sightseeing.\n\n**This is not the event to 
 use to test your fitness level or see how things go.** If you're unsure wh
 ether you can complete the hike\, please choose an easier event instead.\n
 If you find yourself unable to keep up\, you may need to turn back or cont
 inue independently where the route and circumstances allow.\n\nThe group c
 annot stop or slow down significantly to accommodate someone who is strugg
 ling\, as this affects the experience and schedule for everyone.\nPlease m
 ake an honest assessment of your abilities before committing. The goal is 
 to keep the day safe\, enjoyable\, and on track for the entire group.\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🍔 Dinner at Chuck's Roadhouse\n\nAfter the hike\, we'll head t
 o **Chuck's Roadhouse on Clifton Hill** for a relaxed dinner. Everyone is 
 responsible for the cost of their own meal.\n\n⚠️ **Please note:** The
  restaurant has limited vegetarian options. If this means you won't be joi
 ning us for dinner\, please let me know in advance so I can plan the numbe
 rs. Please don't leave this until the last minute\, as I'll be arranging t
 he dinner headcount.\n\n***\n\n## 🎇 Winter Festival of Lights\n\nAfter 
 dinner\, we'll head down to the Falls to enjoy the **Niagara Falls Winter 
 Festival of Lights**.\nThe surrounding area comes alive with illuminated d
 isplays and colourful seasonal installations. We'll take a relaxed evening
  stroll\, enjoy the atmosphere\, and stop for photos along the way.\nBring
  warm layers — temperatures near the Falls can drop\, especially after d
 ark! 🧣✨\n\n***\n\n## 💲 Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 Meetup fee**\n💵 Cash 
 at the event\, or\n📧 E-transfer to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto
 :mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)** before or on the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🚆 TRAN
 SPORTATION REQUIREMENT — PLEASE READ\n\n**Everyone must travel with the 
 group on the GO Train to participate in this event.**\nWe will not meet pe
 ople separately in Niagara Falls. Travelling together helps us coordinate 
 the day's activities\, stay on schedule\, and avoid confusion about meetin
 g points and transportation.\nPlease arrive on time at our Toronto meeting
  point. We will not be able to hold the train for late arrivals.\n\n***\n\
 n## 🕒 Travel Details (Approximate)\n\n* **8:15 AM** — Meet outside th
 e main doors of the Fairmont Royal York on Front Street West. Look for my 
 Moose Hat! 🫎\n* **8:30 AM** — Depart for the GO Train.\n* **9:03 AM**
  — Planned GO Train departure for Niagara Falls.\n* **11:25 AM** — Exp
 ected arrival in Niagara Falls.\n* **12:30 PM** — Planned start of the N
 iagara Glen hike.\n* **4:30 PM** — Dinner at Chuck's Roadhouse.\n* **6:0
 0 PM** — Head down to the Falls for the Winter Festival of Lights.\n* **
 8:00–9:00 PM** — Target return-train window to Toronto.\n\n🚆 These 
 times are approximate and depend on the transit schedule and conditions on
  the day. I'll share any necessary updates closer to the event. Please che
 ck the current GO Transit schedule before purchasing your ticket.\n\n***\n
 \n## 🎟️ Tickets & What to Bring\n\nPlease purchase the **GO + WEGO Co
 mbo Ticket** in advance. The previously listed round-trip price was approx
 imately $20\, but please check the current price and service details befor
 e buying.\n👉 **[Click here for the Niagara Parks GO + WEGO offer](https
 ://www.gotransit.com/en/partners-and-promotions/go-train-to-niagara-on-wee
 kends)**\n\nBring:\n\n* 🥾 Sturdy walking shoes or hiking boots with goo
 d grip.\n* 💧 Water and snacks.\n* 🧥 Warm layers for the evening.\n* 
 📸 A camera or charged phone.\n* 🎒 Anything else you need for a full 
 day outdoors.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n* This is a full\, ac
 tive day involving a train journey\, a hike\, dinner\, and evening sightse
 eing.\n* The event is open to everyone — singles\, couples\, and friends
  — provided they can manage the hike.\n* Please RSVP only if you underst
 and the physical requirements and can commit to the day's itinerary.\n* Yo
 u can RSVP ahead of time or show up on the day if you're unsure about your
  schedule\, but please remember that the train arrangements and group itin
 erary require punctuality.\n* Sometimes things happen and I may need to ca
 ncel or change the plans. Please watch the event page for updates.\n\n***\
 n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or emai
 l **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@h
 otmail.com)**.\n\n**Come for the hike.**\n**Stay for the lights.**\n**Leav
 e with a full day of adventure and new connections.** 🍁🎄
