SUMMARY:🍁 Fall Hike: Long Branch GO to Port Credit GO
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍁 Fall Hike: Long Branch GO t
 o Port Credit GO\n\nJoin us for a scenic lakeside hike along the beautiful
  Waterfront Trail\, from Long Branch GO Station to Port Credit GO Station!
 \n\nWe’ll explore a mix of parks\, beaches\, and tree-lined paths\, taki
 ng in the crisp autumn air\, colourful leaves\, and classic Lake Ontario v
 iews. This is the first time our group has done this particular route\, so
  come along and help us welcome the fall season!\n\nWe’ll take our time\
 , with stops for photos\, snacks\, and conversation along the way. This is
  a social hike rather than a race\, but please be prepared to walk for a f
 ew hours. We’ll finish in Port Credit\, where we’ll take the GO train 
 back toward Toronto.\n\n***\n\n### 🚆 Meetup Details — Choose Your Sta
 rting Point\n\n**Option 1: Meet in Toronto and travel together**\n\n📍 *
 *Meeting location:** Outside the main doors of the Fairmont Royal York on 
 Front Street West.\n\n* **10:15 AM:** Meet outside the hotel. Look for my 
 Moose Hat! 🦌\n* **10:30 AM sharp:** We’ll leave for the station.\n* *
 *10:45 AM:** Planned train departure.\n\nPlease arrive on time. We cannot 
 hold the train for latecomers\, and once we’ve left\, you’ll need to m
 ake your own way to the starting point if you miss us.\n\n**Option 2: Meet
  us at Long Branch GO Station**\n\n📍 **Meeting location:** Long Branch 
 GO Station\, **by the station exit closest to the parking lot**.\n\nThis i
 s our starting point for the hike. Please meet me by that exit and look fo
 r the Moose Hat! 🦌\n\n* **Around 11:00 AM:** Arrive and find the group.
 \n* **11:15 AM:** We’ll begin the walk.\n\nPlease use the specified exit
  rather than waiting elsewhere around the station. We had some confusion w
 ith the meeting point previously\, so make sure you know where to find us.
 \n\n**Important:** This is a point-to-point hike. We’ll finish at **Port
  Credit GO Station**\, not Long Branch. We will not walk back to Long Bran
 ch.\n\n### 🥾 The Walk\n\nWe’ll follow the Waterfront Trail through a 
 mix of waterfront scenery\, parks\, beaches\, and paths. We’ll take occa
 sional breaks for photos\, snacks\, and conversation\, with time to enjoy 
 the views and each other’s company.\n\nPlease wear comfortable walking s
 hoes and be prepared for a few hours on your feet. Bring your own water an
 d snacks\; you’re welcome to bring something extra to share.\n\n### 🚆
  Getting Back\n\nWe expect to start wrapping up around **2:00 PM**\, with 
 our destination being Port Credit GO Station.\n\nWe’ll take the GO train
  from Port Credit toward Toronto. **Please check the GO schedule for the e
 vent date before attending.** Not every train necessarily stops at Long Br
 anch\, so do not assume you can take the train back there to retrieve a ca
 r. If you’re driving and parking at Long Branch\, check your return opti
 ons in advance.\n\n### 💲 Meetup Fee\n\nThe Meetup fee is **$5**\, payab
 le in cash in person or by e-transfer to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mai
 lto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**.\nGO train fares are additional. Check th
 e current fare for your journey.\n\n### 🎒 What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* C
 omfortable walking shoes\n* Snacks or something small for our breaks\n* A 
 camera or phone for the fall colours\n* Weather-appropriate clothing\n\n##
 # ⚠️ Please Note\n\n* This event is weather-dependent only if conditio
 ns make the walk unsafe. Keep an eye on the event page for any updates or 
 cancellation notices.\n* You’re welcome to leave early\, but please let 
 me know so I know you’ve left the group.\n* If you’re joining at Long 
 Branch\, make sure you use the **station exit closest to the parking lot**
 .\n* This is a one-way walk ending at Port Credit. Please plan your transp
 ortation accordingly.\n\n### 👥 About the Group\n\nWhether you’re sing
 le or partnered\, you’re welcome to join us to get outdoors\, meet peopl
 e\, and make connections. We also organize movies\, walks\, hikes\, arts a
 nd culture outings\, restaurant visits\, and plenty more.\nOrganized by Ma
 thew. Questions? Post on the event wall or email **[torontomoviesandouting
 s@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\n🍁 Enjo
 y the trail. Take in the views. Meet some new people.
