SUMMARY:🌰 Hogg’s Hollow Fall Walk & Lunch! 🍂!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n### 🌰 Hogg’s Hollow Fall Walk
  & Lunch! 🍂\n\nJoin us for a beautiful fall walk through Hogg’s Hollo
 w\, one of Toronto’s charming historic neighbourhoods tucked away in Nor
 th York. With its winding roads\, forested trails\, stone bridges\, and sc
 enic ravines\, this area feels like a hidden village in the middle of the 
 city — especially when the leaves turn golden and the air starts to feel
  like autumn.\n\nWe’ll explore the valley around the Don River West Bran
 ch\, taking in the neighbourhood’s natural beauty and historic character
 . Along the way\, we’ll touch on the story of James Hogg\, the Scottish 
 settler associated with the area’s early mill\, and the tragic **Hogg’
 s Hollow Disaster of 1960**\, when five workers lost their lives during tu
 nnel construction.\n\nAfter our walk\, we’ll head to **Swiss Chalet** fo
 r lunch\, because nothing says fall like comfort food and good company! 
 🍗\n\n### 📍 Meetup Location — Please Read Carefully!\n\n**We’re m
 eeting directly in front of the Shell gas station store entrance.**\nPleas
 e stand **right in front of the entrance to the store**\, where people wal
 k in and out.\nLook for my famous Moose Hat! 🦌\n\n### 🕒 Meetup Detai
 ls\n\n* **Meeting time:** 11:00 AM\n* **Departure:** 11:05 AM sharp. I’l
 l wait a maximum of five minutes.\n* **Ending location:** We’ll return t
 o our starting point\, making it convenient for anyone arriving by transit
  or car.\n* **Meetup fee:** $5\, payable in cash or by e-transfer to **[ma
 thewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**.\n\n### 🥾 
 What to Bring\n\n* Water\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* A snack if you’
 d like something before lunch\n* Weather-appropriate clothing\n\n☔ **Rai
 n or shine!** There’s no such thing as bad weather — just inappropriat
 e clothing.\n\n### 👥 About the Group\n\nWhether you’re single or part
 nered\, you’re welcome to join us to get outdoors\, meet people\, and ma
 ke connections. We also organize movies\, walks\, hikes\, arts and culture
  outings\, restaurant visits\, and plenty more.\n**You can RSVP ahead of t
 ime or show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it.\n\nOrgan
 ized by Mathew. Questions? Post on the event wall or email **[torontomovie
 sandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**.\n\
 n🍂 Enjoy the walk. Stay for lunch. Leave with new connections.
